There it is! `coblocal.h`:

```c
#define COB_D2I(x)		((x) - '0')
#define COB_I2D(x)		(char) ((x) + '0')
```

So COB_D2I(x) = x - '0' — an unconditional ASCII minus '0' (no digit check!). This confirms that the conversion treats every byte as `byte - '0'` (space = 32-48 = -16?? Wait, that contradicts the observation for T1!).

